        "sender_principal_id": "human",
        "worker_id": null,
        "execution_id": null,
        "body": "DIRECT_PRIVATE_SENTINEL_P08. In this private conversation, compare a discussion recommendation with an implementation assignment. Ask Grace one bounded peer question about a concrete failure mode if these are confused, using ask_peer; do not invent her answer. After the bounded peer response, explain the practical distinction and uncertainty. No Tasks, source edits or external actions.",
        "request_id": null,
        "response_to": null,
        "created_at": "2026-10-05T19:47:12.902Z"
      },
      {
        "cursor": 17,
        "message_id": "cmessage_51c8a672-573c-4ea5-811f-216720bd3409",
        "conversation_id": "conversation_26cf3990-ba26-4f23-a809-d3f86a7eead7",
        "sender_principal_id": "principal_c347e1e2-0693-4d69-aadc-d374ab0cf136",
        "worker_id": "worker_0e23d704-3661-49b1-a05d-0d4f3cdb5d77",
        "execution_id": "execution_6449677d-6b7e-4ca6-b79d-ee5a5db0599d",
        "body": "I asked Grace for one concrete failure mode if a discussion recommendation is mistaken for an authorized implementation assignment. Her response is pending, so I won’t attribute an answer to her yet.\n\nThe practical distinction is authority: a recommendation proposes an option for consideration; an implementation assignment explicitly authorizes a defined owner to act within a stated scope. Confusing them can lead to unapproved work or a false expectation that work is underway. I have not created a Task, edited source, or taken an external action.",
        "request_id": "reply_414f5257-7ba2-407c-af84-634048a65942",
        "response_to": "reply_414f5257-7ba2-407c-af84-634048a65942",
        "created_at": "2026-10-05T19:47:26.676Z"
      },
      {
        "cursor": 19,
        "message_id": "cmessage_ab57ae08-9f45-4c41-800e-a6e253491755",
        "conversation_id": "conversation_26cf3990-ba26-4f23-a809-d3f86a7eead7",
        "sender_principal_id": "human",
        "worker_id": null,
        "execution_id": null,
        "body": "Retain this passive constraint: raw diagnostic logs expire after 48 hours; the tombstone policy remains unresolved.",
        "request_id": null,
        "response_to": null,
        "created_at": "2026-10-05T19:48:24.045Z"
      },
      {
        "cursor": 20,
        "message_id": "cmessage_d650058b-41eb-46fd-9813-cf43fe6e1a07",
        "conversation_id": "conversation_26cf3990-ba26-4f23-a809-d3f86a7eead7",
        "sender_principal_id": "human",
        "worker_id": null,
        "execution_id": null,
        "body": "After context replacement, recover the passive 48-hour log constraint and unresolved tombstone question. Explain how a group recommendation differs from an implementation assignment; no Task or code changes.",
        "request_id": null,
        "response_to": null,
        "created_at": "2026-10-05T19:48:26.184Z"
      },
      {
        "cursor": 21,
        "message_id": "cmessage_243ef1e0-07f6-4c9a-bc90-9a0fab7dc0e6",
        "conversation_id": "conversation_26cf3990-ba26-4f23-a809-d3f86a7eead7",
        "sender_principal_id": "principal_c347e1e2-0693-4d69-aadc-d374ab0cf136",
        "worker_id": "worker_0e23d704-3661-49b1-a05d-0d4f3cdb5d77",
        "execution_id": "execution_e5fb9ca9-1217-44f5-bafe-477ff3910eb4",
        "body": "Recovered constraint: raw diagnostic logs expire after 48 hours. The tombstone policy remains an open question; I won’t infer a retention or deletion rule for tombstones.\n\nA group recommendation is advice for consideration, not authorization to execute. An implementation assignment would identify an authorized owner, scope, and expected action. Treating the recommendation as an assignment risks unapproved work or a misleading claim that work is underway. I have made no Task or code changes.",
        "request_id": "reply_9f2d08ba-6fad-4866-9df4-050817eb4d26",
        "response_to": "reply_9f2d08ba-6fad-4866-9df4-050817eb4d26",
        "created_at": "2026-10-05T19:48:34.664Z"
      },
      {
